<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> "Network Protocol"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> "OSI Reference Model"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> "Ontology Design Pattern"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "ISO/IEC 7498-1 Ontology Design Pattern"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498> <http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/doi> "10.1109/ETFA61755.2024.10710890" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498> <http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/status> "Draft"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "iso7498" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498#" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Normative basis: ISO/IEC 7498-1:1994.\r\n\r\nTwenty-six classes and four relations. Every definition carries a German wording alongside its English translation.\r\n\r\nThe layers, the technologies and the kinds of data unit are modelled as subclasses.\r\n\r\nScope: the layered structure of a communication and what travels over it. The open system with its subsystems and entities, services and protocols, the transmission modes and the quality of service are not covered."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.0.0" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/fundedBy> <https://dtecbw.de/> .
